hey this is presh talwalkar and you're  watching mind your decisions  today stanford ranks as one of the top  universities in the world  in this video let's take a trip back in  time  can you solve the stanford entrance exam  questions from 1892  here's a trigonometry question  express tangent squared of theta plus  cotangent squared of theta in terms of  cosine theta  here's an advanced algebra question  if a b and c are in harmonical  progression  prove b plus a all over b minus a plus b  plus c all over b minus c is equal to 2.  can you figure it out  give these problems a try and when  you're ready keep watching the video for  a solution  so the trigonometry question is pretty  straightforward  tangent of theta is equal to sine of  theta over cosine of theta and the  cotangent of theta is the reciprocal of  that  we substitute these in to tangent  squared of theta plus cotangent squared  of theta  and now all we need to do is simplify  sine squared of theta in terms of cosine  of theta  we can do this with the identity sine  squared of theta is equal to one minus  cosine squared of theta  and when we substitute that in that's  about as simplified as we can get  we have one minus cosine squared of  theta all over cosine squared of theta  plus cosine squared of theta all over  one minus cosine squared of theta  so now let's go to the algebra question  the key part of this question  is what is a harmonic progression  i personally did not know this and i'll  admit i had to look it up  in a harmonic progression the  denominators are in an arithmetic  progression so if the first term is one  over x  the next term is one over x plus d  then the next term is one over x plus  two d  then we have one over x plus three d and  so on each time we're adding this common  difference of d to the denominator  so we might as well say that a is equal  to one over x b is equal to one over x  plus d and c is equal to one over x plus  two d for some common difference d  so we'll take this and we'll substitute  it in and see if we can simplify our  expression  so we first do b plus a all over b minus  a  we get a kind of complicated fraction  but we can simplify it with a little  trick  we'll multiply the numerator and  denominator by the quantity x plus d  times x  this simplifies the numerator to be x  plus the quantity x plus d and the  denominator becomes x minus the quantity  x plus d  the numerator becomes 2x plus d and the  denominator becomes a negative d  so we have the opposite  of the fraction 2x plus d all over d  now let's simplify b plus c over b minus  c  we'll substitute in our terms of the  harmonic progression  and now we'll use the same trick to  simplify  we'll multiply the numerator and  denominator by the quantity x plus d  multiplied by the quantity x plus 2d  the numerator becomes x plus 2d plus the  quantity x plus d and the denominator  becomes x plus 2d minus the quantity x  plus d  this simplifies to be 2x plus 3d all  over d  so now we need to add these two terms  together  so when we do that we actually cancel  out these two x terms  and then we get 2d all over d  which simplifies to be 2.  so we've proven that this expression  simplifies to be two  did you figure it out  thanks for watching this video these  math videos which can be watched for  free on youtube inspire and build  confidence for people around the world  and they already have over a hundred  million views let's share the beauty of  mathematics with your help we can map  the world a better place  please subscribe for free to the news  videos watch and share all of mind your  decisions videos email me a puzzle presh  mind yourdecisions.com  if you so choose you can check out my  books which are listed in the video  description and you can support me on  patreon for exclusive rewards thanks for  watching and thanks for your support
 

